    "body": "## Summary\n\nHardens the Stripe dispute/chargeback lifecycle against out-of-order webhook delivery.\n\n- Flyway V53 persists a `stripe_state_event_created_at` provider-state watermark.\n- Signed Stripe `Event.created` is forwarded from the webhook controller into dispute settlement.\n- Provider status/reason metadata cannot be regressed by an older event.\n- Immutable charge identity is still validated even for stale events.\n- Same-second delivery cannot replace an already terminal Stripe dispute status with a different status.\n- Financial `funds_withdrawn` / `funds_reinstated` signals remain independently event-idempotent and are not discarded merely because provider metadata is stale.\n- Historical disputes establish their watermark on the next valid signed event.\n- Unit coverage and dispute lifecycle documentation are updated.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nDo not merge until every PR-triggered workflow for the exact latest head SHA is green, the branch is 0 behind `master`, and the PR remains mergeable. Merge method must be a merge commit with an expected-head guard.",
